---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { meta } from "../../data/pages";
import registry from "../../../public/registry/v1/index.json";
import descriptions from "../../data/plugin-copy.json";
import { pluginMCP } from "../../data/mcp";
import InstallCommand from "../../components/InstallCommand.astro";
const copy: Record<string, { title: string; description: string; guide: string }> = descriptions;
const featuredOrder = ["pii", "usage_logger", "pii_guard"];
const plugins = [...registry.plugins].sort((left, right) => {
  const leftPriority = featuredOrder.indexOf(left.name);
  const rightPriority = featuredOrder.indexOf(right.name);
  if (leftPriority !== -1 || rightPriority !== -1) {
    if (leftPriority === -1) return 1;
    if (rightPriority === -1) return -1;
    return leftPriority - rightPriority;
  }
  return left.name.localeCompare(right.name);
});
---
<Layout {...meta("/plugins/")}>
  <section class="frame prose plugin-catalogue" style="max-width:var(--page)">
    <h1 class="display">Pick a plugin. Make it yours.</h1>
    <p>Check tool output, track usage, change routing, or shape context. Install a maintained plugin by name—no Git or Go needed—then review its permissions and enable it in your local control plane.</p>
    <div class="first-choice">
      <p><strong>Have a local model?</strong><br />Try <a href="#pii">model-backed PII checks</a> alongside your hosted agent.</p>
      <p><strong>No local model?</strong><br />Start with <a href="#usage_logger">usage logging</a> or <a href="#pii_guard">deterministic checks</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <nav class="plugin-index" aria-label="Jump to a plugin">{plugins.map(plugin => <a href={`#${plugin.name}`}>{plugin.name}</a>)}</nav>
    <div>
      {plugins.map((plugin) => (
        <article class="plugin-detail" id={plugin.name}>
          <p class="plugin-name"><code>{plugin.name}</code></p>
          <h2>{copy[plugin.name].title}</h2>
          <p>{copy[plugin.name].description}</p>
          <InstallCommand command={`torana plugin install ${plugin.name}`} label={`install command for ${plugin.name}`} analyticsCopy="plugin-install" />
          <div class="actions"><a class="button" href={copy[plugin.name].guide}>Setup guide ↗</a><a class="button" href={plugin.source}>Source ↗</a></div>
          {pluginMCP[plugin.name] && <details>
            <summary>Agent tools via MCP</summary>
            <p><strong>Agent tools via MCP</strong> — {pluginMCP[plugin.name].description}</p>
            <p>{pluginMCP[plugin.name].operations.map((operation, index) => <>{index > 0 && " · "}<code>{operation}</code></>)} · <a href="/docs/mcp/#operations">MCP guide →</a></p>
          </details>}
          <p class="article-meta">On plugin failure: {plugin.failure_mode === "block" ? "block the request" : "let the request continue"}.</p>
          {plugin.conflicts_with.length > 0 && <p>Use separately from: {plugin.conflicts_with.join(", ")}.</p>}
          <details>
            <summary>Requested capabilities ({plugin.capabilities.length})</summary>
            <ul class="capabilities">{plugin.capabilities.map(capability => <li>{capability}</li>)}</ul>
            <p>These are the manifest’s requests, not automatic grants. Review resource bindings and the exact built digest in the control plane.</p>
          </details>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
    <h2>Make it your own.</h2>
    <p>Your plugin can live in your own repository. Move a harness-specific extension into a reusable plugin, then <a href="/plugins/submit/">share it for a catalogue listing</a>. For permissions, version pinning and source builds, see the <a href="/docs/plugin-installation/">installation guide</a>. <a href="/docs/mcp/">Connect MCP</a> to let your agent discover plugin tools.</p>
    <details><summary>Registry API and release verification</summary>
    <pre><code>GET https://torana.sh/registry/v1/index.json</code></pre>
    <p>The <a href="/registry/v1/index.json">registry</a> lists plugin source, manifest declarations and independently published release digests. Torana downloads release bundles from GitHub and checks them against these digests. Installation never grants permissions. <a href="/docs/plugin-installation/#digests">How bundle verification works →</a></p>
    </details>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .plugin-catalogue > p { max-width: 68ch; }
  .first-choice { display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); margin-block: var(--space-5); }
  .first-choice p { margin: 0; padding-inline-start: var(--space-4); border-inline-start: 2px solid var(--accent); }
  .plugin-index { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-2) var(--space-5); border-block: 1px solid var(--rule); padding-block: var(--space-3); margin-block-end: var(--space-7); }
  .plugin-index a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: .85rem; white-space: nowrap; }
  .plugin-name { margin: 0 0 var(--space-2); font-size: .85rem; }
  .plugin-detail h2 { max-width: 32ch; font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3vw, 2.25rem); line-height: 1.15; }
  .plugin-detail .actions { margin-block: var(--space-4); }
  @media (min-width: 48rem) { .first-choice { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; } }
</style>
